 ## Overview
 
-Piecewise Linear Interpolation (Lookup Table) is the standard method for evaluating 1D transfer functions in volume rendering, mapping scalar data values to visual parameters (color and opacity) by interpolating between user-defined control points [S1, S2, S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of converting discrete user interactions into continuous visual mappings by constructing a continuous curve from a set of anchor points [S2, S7, unofficial]. It differs from [Cubic Spline Transfer Function](1811-cubic-spline-transfer-function.md) by lacking derivative continuity at segment boundaries, which can lead to visual artifacts like ringing in derived geometries [S9].
