 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Transfer Function Control Point Management](2718-transfer-function-control-point-management.md)
-Transfer Function Control Point Management handles the insertion, deletion, modification, and sorting of control points that define a piecewise linear transfer function (TF). It solves the problem of maintaining a valid, sorted domain (ascending scalar values) and consistent data structures during interactive user manipulation (dragging, clicking, deleting). It distinguishes itself from [Blurring a Step Function](4383-blurring-a-step-function.md) and [Step Function Resampling](7924-step-function-resampling.md) by operating on the parametric control points themselves rather than the resulting discrete lookup table (LUT) values, ensuring topological correctness (no crossing points) before interpolation.
