 ### [Step Function Resampling](7924-step-function-resampling.md)
-Step Function Resampling constructs inner and outer measures on a step function to resample values defined by endpoints into new intervals. It solves the problem of aggregating piecewise-constant data (such as transfer function weights or probability mass) over arbitrary query ranges, providing both the exact sum (outer measure) and the guaranteed contained mass (inner measure). It preserves the discontinuous nature of the source data rather than interpolating between control points, unlike [Piecewise Linear Interpolation (Lookup Table)](2643-piecewise-linear-interpolation-lookup-table.md), and provides exact bounds rather than smoothed approximations, unlike [Blurring a Step Function](4383-blurring-a-step-function.md).
